      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$ is\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$",
